{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_EthSwt_00087","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_EthSwt_00087@rel:R19-11#e07e22ad","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_EthSwt_00087","release":"R19-11","content":"The function EthSwt_StoreConfiguration shall store the configuration of the learned MAC/Port tables of a switch in a persistent manner. This can be done in two ways: 1.) Reading out the parameters and storing them in the NV-RAM of the host CPU using the NV-RAM manager. 2.) Advising the switch to store the configuration data in its local NV-RAM.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_EthernetSwitchDriver.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:18+00:00"},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_EthSwt_00087@rel:R20-11#9f56d5bd","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_EthSwt_00087","release":"R20-11","content":"The function EthSwt_StoreConfiguration shall request to store the configuration of the learned MAC/Port tables of a switch in a persistent manner. This can be done in two ways: 1.) Reading out the parameters and storing them in the NV-RAM of the host CPU using the NV-RAM manager. 2.) Advising the switch to store the configuration data in its local NV-RAM. In both alternatives <EthSwtPersistentConfigurationResultCallback> shall be invoked if EthSwtPersistentConfigurationResultCallback is configured. In case of storage to switch local NV-RAM, JobResult shall be set to NVM_REQ_OK to indicate success or to NVM_REQ_NOT_OK to indicate failure.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_EthernetSwitchDriver.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:36+00:00"},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_EthSwt_00087@rel:R21-11#9f56d5bd","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_EthSwt_00087","release":"R21-11","content":"The function EthSwt_StoreConfiguration shall request to store the configuration of the learned MAC/Port tables of a switch in a persistent manner. This can be done in two ways: 1.) Reading out the parameters and storing them in the NV-RAM of the host CPU using the NV-RAM manager. 2.) Advising the switch to store the configuration data in its local NV-RAM. In both alternatives <EthSwtPersistentConfigurationResultCallback> shall be invoked if EthSwtPersistentConfigurationResultCallback is configured. In case of storage to switch local NV-RAM, JobResult shall be set to NVM_REQ_OK to indicate success or to NVM_REQ_NOT_OK to indicate failure.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_EthernetSwitchDriver.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:13:01+00:00"},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_EthSwt_00087@rel:R22-11#cb990e4e","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_EthSwt_00087","release":"R22-11","content":"The function EthSwt_StoreConfiguration shall request to store the configuration of the learned MAC/Port tables of a switch in a persistent manner. This can be done in two ways: 1.) Reading out the parameters and storing 83 of 212 Document ID 656: AUTOSAR_SWS_EthernetSwitchDriver Specification of Ethernet Switch Driver AUTOSAR CP R22-11 them in the NV-RAM of the host CPU using the NV-RAM manager. 2.) Advising the switch to store the configuration data in its local NV-RAM. In both alternatives <EthSwtPersistentConfigurationResultCallback> shall be invoked if EthSwtPersistentConfigurationResultCallback is configured. In case of storage to switch local NV-RAM, JobResult shall be set to NVM_REQ_OK to indi- cate success or to NVM_REQ_NOT_OK to indicate failure.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_EthernetSwitchDriver.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:13:22+00:00"},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_EthSwt_00087","release":"R23-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_EthSwt_00087","release":"R24-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_